- FoundrySoftHQ/agent-for-accounting, 7a9e8f9a81eb314b70418051b75213cf6230a01f

The new instructions and fabricated validation cards are independently
written. No upstream code, guide bodies, corpus text, rate tables, email
access or hosted-service integration is imported.

The short-stay accommodation topic gap, the contract-date CGT timing card and
a test against hard-coded figures in skill prose were identified on
15 October 2026 by reviewing the MIT-licensed darrentmorgan/au-accounting,
commit 8576474dbe0c. The au-short-stay-accommodation workflow and its cards
are independently written from ATO, legislation and State Revenue Office
Victoria sources read that day, and tests/test_skill_figures.py is
independently written. No upstream skill text,
evaluation case, code, rates data or refusal codes were copied.

The idea of a pre-lodgement review list came from the published feature list
of william-laverty/ato-mcp (AGPL-3.0), commit aa0d341bbca4, on 15 October
2026. The au-pre-lodgement-review workflow is an original design written
from ATO sources; no ato-mcp code, schemas, prompts or prose were used.

The idea of a reconciliation break-trace workflow, with a one-sentence cause
per break and a diagnose-only boundary, came from the break-trace skill in
the Apache-2.0-licensed anthropics/financial-services, commit
574ed3624aeb, read on 20 October 2026. The reconciliation-break-trace
workflow and its cards are independently written for Australian practice
ledgers; no upstream skill text, prompts, schemas or code were copied.

The topics of 16 skills added on 2 November 2026, and of 5 extensions, were
identified by comparing the public skill list at
https://nagaris.com/ask-nagaris-skills, read that day. The page publishes only
skill names and one-line descriptions; no Nagaris text was copied. The new
workflows and cards are independently written from Australian primary
sources. The comparison is recorded in docs/nagaris-comparison.md.

The topics of 4 skills added on 4 November 2026 were identified from public
material; no text from it was copied. au-client-departure and au-trust-losses
come from the public titles of CA ANZ member resources, including its N1
guidance note on client records and a members-only trust losses checklist
that was not read. au-ato-correspondence-triage and
au-ato-account-reconciliation come from the public product descriptions of
Business Automation Works' ATOmate and Omble, read on 3 November 2026, and the
year-end list of ATO amendments processed after balance date from the idea of
LodgeiT's True Balance Validator help article, read on 4 November 2026. The
workflows and cards are independently written from APESB, TPB, ATO and Federal
Register of Legislation sources; CA ANZ's N1 and CR 3 are cited as member
guidance and regulation.

The topics of au-main-residence and au-share-buy-back, added on 11 November
2026, come from the same public Ask Nagaris skill list, read again on
11 November 2026. No Nagaris text was copied. The workflows and cards are
independently written from Federal Register of Legislation, ATO and ASIC
sources.
